  "term": "medical psychology",
  "definition": "Medical psychology is the study of abnormal and diseased mental states and their symptoms, considered chiefly from a medical viewpoint. In historical usage, the term was closely connected with psychological medicine and related to psychiatry, psychopathology, and mental pathology.",
